Evidence policy:
  Earlier development runs used intermediate source snapshots. They informed
  model design but are not used as final evidence here. The retained
  production outputs above all use the recorded final source hash.

Conclusion:
  No sequence of length at most 70 was found.
  No global impossibility proof was produced.
  UNKNOWN results are timeouts, not evidence of unsatisfiability.
  The one INFEASIBLE status concerns only a single disjoint distinct-support
  anchor case and does not change the public bound.
  The support-69 run covers one repeated-window stage and one anchor partition
  only. The remaining support sizes and anchors are unresolved.
  A lower bound of 71 would require complete proof evidence for every
  admissible length from 62 through 70, including all repeated-window cases.
